Z||000000||danny boy||06-11-2001||08:19 PM|||| Some group was picketting the McVeigh excecution saying it wasn't right.  B.S.!!!! What should we do with poeple like that? Put them in prision,clothe and feed them well, and use our tax money to do it all? Hell no. In light of a protest because they said it was "cruel and unusual punishment", I have came up with another way to do it. <BR>    Ok, first we need a stadium. Football, baseball or even a purpose built place, as long as it didn't have a roof. Grass field with 10'x110' squares painted on it,each numbered.<BR>    Charge admission for seats and have a betting booth for the gambling patrons. A bet will be placed on any number on the field. A plane will fly over the stadium at approximately 5,000' and when over the field the executionee will be thrown from the plane. What are the numbers on the field and the betting for? Which square the guy(or girl) is gonna land in.<BR> Boy, that'd get those "just because he performed the worst terrorist attack on US soil is no reason to kill him"  crybaby ashos goin wouldn't it? I'd like to take their signs and beat them with them. Almost as bad as PETA, which by the way stands for People Eat The Animals. We are at the top of the food chain, deal with it.<P> So has anyone have any Ideas of their own?<P>------------------<BR>don't push the A/c button.. it catches the car on fire        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||06-11-2001||08:30 PM||||I'm not sure if I'm for or against capital punishment.  "Thou shalt not kill" should include everybody, but there needs to be some sort of ultimate punishment for ultimate crimes.  Timothy McVeigh wasn't remorsefull even at the very end.  (His, "I'm sorry people had to die" speach was total BS.)  How about "an eye for an eye" (which is usually taken out of context)?  If you rape someone, you get raped yourself.  If you blow someone up, you get to eat a grenade.  I just don't know.  No matter what someone's stand on capital punishment is, it's still a waste of a life (not that I think he could have been rehabilitated).<P>MM||||reg||1
