Z||000005||87 Pegasus||06-11-2001||11:16 PM||||tease the facker.  put him in the gas chamber..get it going.  just when he thinks it's the end, put the exhaust fans on and air it out.  Do this a couple of times, then put him back.  The next day, put him in the chair.  Get some juice going.  Work him up to the point of EXCRUCIATING pain...then stop.  Put him back for the night.  The next day, hang him.  But don't pull something out from under him.  Don't want that precious neck to break.  Let his eyes bulge and his face turn blue.  Then let him down.  Put him back.  Next day, tie him to a pole in front of a firing squad.  Have them miss a couple times, then maybe just wing him.  Then start shooting various limbs...legs, arms, go for the kneecaps.  Then put him back.  Make sure the precious boy doesn't bleed to death.  Finally, bring him out to a surgery table.  Gut the facker and hang him above his own self so he can see what made him.  Even all that will not amount to HALF the pain he caused, but it may appease some.............don't you want to piss me off?  HA!!!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Friends don't let friends drive Corvettes!!||||reg||10
Z||000006||stimpy||06-12-2001||12:09 AM||||I'm against capital punishment especially in this case. It's far too easy. He'll spend eternity in hell, why rush it?  I think that McVeigh should have been comitted to be subject to medical experimentation. Give that piece of garbage cancer and try to cure it. Test tear gas and pepper spray and the effect on testicular tissue. Test new skin grafting techniques by taking a blowtorch to him. All kinds of Gestapo sh!t. Milk it out for a good 50 years or so.||||reg||1
Z||000007||DaRkLoRD||06-12-2001||12:17 AM||||I still haven't heard one good reason of WHY he targeted that particular building for his attack.. but in general, how could an execution possibly cost more than housing a criminal for years??<P>Ok, here's my stand on the issue... I think if a person intentionally commits an UNPROVOKED violent crime, the death penalty should be used, once the suspect has been proven guilty beyond all doubt. Why keep the person around? In the case of an obviously provoked attack, such as when a person is mistreated and bullied for years until they finally snap... I think rehabilitation is in order if they're stopped before they kill anyone.. if not.. then I don't know.<P>the one thing that hardly ever happens in this situation, is an investigation into the actions of the people that provoked the suspect..... recently at my old high school, a student who had been bullied created a hit list, and planned on raiding the school to kill the people who had been tormenting him. The police found out about this and arrested him, and have also pressed some charges against the person who has been mistreating the guy. this was handled much better than the other cases I heard of in the states.. in fact, shortly after the columbine situation, many schools were encouraged to have students report "antisocial" behaviour, ie. unpopular and/or bullied geeks, in case they snapped.. what about having people report bullies instead of victims that are about to fight back? something's wrong there.<P>sorry this got off topic.. heh.. lethal injection is fine, but for really nasty guys, I say give them a ton of stimulants so they CAN'T lose consciousness... and then start cutting them up... heh.. (I honestly can't think of too many people that would deserve that..)<P>whew that was long.<P>p.s. the idea for the torture execution I mentioned I actually got from doing research into some experiments the US Government had allegedly done in the 1960s.. Instead of cutting people up, they just subjected them to pain until the person mentally snapped and formed a new personality, sort of like an artificial way of creating multiple personality disorder. This new personality would be hypnotically "programmed" to commit an act, and then it was suppressed and the person didn't remember anything until a trigger word (set with a hypnotic suggestion) was used to "wake up" this new personality. This program was called, among other names, "MKULTRA", and the movie Conspiracy Theory was partly based on it.<P>------------------<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>     <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 06-14-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000008||JSocha||06-12-2001||12:28 AM||||No! No! No! No! No!<P>PETA = "People Eat Tasty Animals"!  <P>That's what I always tell people who are always trying to save the beef, pork, chickens and what ever else can land tastefully on my dinner plate.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||AusFiero||06-12-2001||05:41 AM||||I agree that quick was too good for him. They shoulda set little bombs all over him and blew of a small bit at a time. you know a finger, then a toe, maybe the end of his dick next etc etc.<P>I know he did something horrible but do you think he might have been suffering effects from fighting in the Gulf War. Many Vietnam vets in Aus are pretty f***ed up in the head one way or another. Not all but many. How about over there? Wondering if it got to him too.<P>We have a serial killer locked away here for life for the Port Arthur Massacre(sicko went hunting in a place full of tourists and just killed anyone he came across)...The authorities have stopped him killing himself twice. Why I will never know.<P>Not that I am a real advocate of the death penalty but an eye for an eye works for ancient tribes so why not us.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||8
Z||000010||stimpy||06-12-2001||09:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR><B>I still haven't heard one good reason of WHY he targeted that particular building for his attack.. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>There were some special programs on MSNBC last night that shed some light on that. McVeigh and Nichols considered targets in California, Texas, Arkansas, Washington DC, and rejected them all for some reason.<P>The Murrah building was attractive for several reasons. It is in the "Heartland" of the USA. OKC is the crossroads of U.S., with major north/south and east/west Interstates.  The Murrah also housed many of the same ATF agents that participated in the Branch Davidian siege.  One particuarly nefarious reason was that it would look good for the TV cameras. Plenty of good sight lines from neighboring lots, plus the Murrah was bigger then any surronding building which increased it's visual impact. <BR>Also, the Murrah was very easy to get to. McVeigh was able to drive it right up to the front door. ||||reg||1
