Z||000043||Voytek||06-15-2001||02:40 PM||||I think most of you are a bunch of sickos.  First, let me make my position clear: I AM for HUMANE capital punishment.<BR>Black88GT: An excellent point: many murderers (eg. OJ Simpson) get off because of their money.  Timothy McVeigh?  Probably would not have got the death penalty if he had a team of good lawyers and claimed to be an 'oppressed' black person (nothing against our black brothers intended).<BR>LZeitgeist:  I'm with you on this one.  Here are a bunch of people who think of themselves as civilized, coming up with more elaborate ways to execute people than serial killers themselves.  Some of you probably intended to joke around (not very funny), to others: give your heads a shake!<BR>Going back to this TM thing, do you all think that you have all the facts on what TM did?  Do you REALLY belive that the gov't and media disclosed absolutely everything to the public?  While I in NO WAY support what this man did, I find it VERY hard to believe that he was completely alone in this.  ESPECIALLY finding out that the FBI had hidden some evidence from the defense, which came to light just a few weeks ago.  What was that evidence??  How come no one mentioned it again??  What happened to the said 'accomplices' that McVeight supposedly had?  My point is, most of you seem so damn sure about the cruelest possible punishments but you never stop to think what's behind the crimes.<BR>I am also against the 'spectacle' they make out of an execution.  A couple of witnesses is fine just to say 'yes, he died', but inviting 3 ROOMS FULL OF PEOPLE TO WATCH??!!  What's next, pay-per-view???!!  And after that?  If enough money is collected, maybe we'll start executing more people, and maybe for lesser crimes at $30 or $40 bucks per show!!??  Mass murderers should be executed only as a preventative measure and because they pose a threat to the society, not because of 'eye-for-an-eye' or to inflict torture.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
